FEATURE: auto-writer-fixes
DATE: 2026-08-26
SCOPE: repair the AutoWriter module; every directive and every path off the happy path
ORIGIN: verification of vUX-autoWriter.js, which had not been revised since 2021-07-19

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AFFECTED PROJECTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

vUX library (this repository) — the only project affected.

  - vUX-autoWriter.js   the AutoWriter constructor, rewritten internally

No other module imports AutoWriter, the repository contains no example page for it, and
doc/README.md still lists its guide as "coming next", so nothing in the repository
depended on the behaviour that changed.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT WAS WRONG
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Plain typing and the '|' line-break directive worked. Almost everything else did not.
Fourteen defects were confirmed by executing the module, four of them severe enough to
break ordinary use:

  1. The '~n~' delay directive threw and stopped typing dead under the DEFAULT
     configuration, because resumeWriting() dereferenced a blinker node that only
     exists when config.showCursor is true.
  2. An unterminated '~' or '*' directive froze the browser tab and then crashed it:
     both scanners looped past the end of the string with no bounds test.
  3. An instance could not be used twice. A second writeText() ignored its arguments,
     wrote the literal string "undefined", and retyped the first string into the first
     element.
  4. The collection ("multiple") mode had never run. writeText() validated argument 1
     as an Element before consulting the type test, rejecting every collection.

The rest: deleteText() erased n+1 units and accepted a non-integer count that left an
interval erasing for ever; erasing popped characters off innerHTML and so shredded tags
("A<br/>B" became "A<br"); the inline '*n*' directive raced its own erasing; a trailing
directive emitted "undefined"; a partial config.cursorStyle blanked the members it did
not name; omitting the optional callback relied on the browser eval'ing the string
"null"; timers leaked; and there was no way to cancel a run.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT CHANGED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Internals, in ten changes recorded in logs/vUX-autoWriter.js_ai_change.log:

  - one bounded directive reader replaces the two unbounded scanners, and the whole
    string is verified by writeText() up front, so a malformed directive throws to its
    caller like any other argument fault instead of failing inside a timer
  - typing and erasing work on DOM nodes instead of innerHTML strings, so a line break
    is one erasable unit and markup is never re-parsed or truncated mid-tag
  - one step machine drives all four paths (character, '|', '*n*', '~n~') and returns
    through the same bounds test every tick; the erase directive resumes typing from a
    completion callback rather than racing it
  - per-run state is built at the start and cleared at the end, which makes an instance
    reusable and collapses the single/group split into one list of boxes and texts
  - the type test runs first and owns argument validation, which makes collection mode
    reachable and lets it accept an HTMLCollection or a plain array, not only a NodeList
  - all four timers are tracked and cleared together

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC API
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Unchanged, and one addition:

  writeText(textBox, text, fn)    same signature; now also accepts a collection of
                                  elements with an array of strings, as the module
                                  always intended but never permitted
  deleteText(n, textBox, fn)      same signature; now erases exactly n
  config.*                        same five properties, same meanings
  stop()                          NEW — cancels a run in progress and clears its timers

Behavioural differences a consumer could notice, all of them corrections:

  - a malformed '*n*' or '~n~' directive now throws from writeText() instead of hanging
  - deleteText(n) removes n units, not n+1
  - a second writeText() on the same instance clears the target span and types the text
    it was given, rather than appending to the previous run
  - a line break is a real <br> element rather than the parsed remains of a "<br/>"
    string; visually identical, and now erasable as one unit

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOT DONE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  - src/helpers.js validateInteger() still returns a boolean rather than throwing,
    which silently disables its use here and in $$.randomInteger. Worked around locally
    in this module; the shared fix wants its own feature entry.
  - AutoWriter remains undocumented (no doc/auto-writer.md) and has no example page.
    doc/README.md line 33 still lists its guide as pending. Out of scope for a repair.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The repository has no test runner, no build step and no dev server, so the module was
exercised directly against a stubbed core ($$, the validateX family, processAssetPath,
vModel) and a minimal DOM. Every defect was measured on the old file and re-measured on
the new one. 26 assertions pass, covering all ten changes and the behaviour that already
worked. The harness is scratch, not committed.
